CORE gcc-only
main.c
--arch riscv64 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^ *CALL __asm_mfence\(\)$
^ *CALL __asm_lfence\(\)$
^ *CALL __asm_sfence\(\)$
^ *CALL __asm_fstcw\(cast\(address_of\(main::1::cw\), empty\*\)\)$
^ *CALL __asm_fldcw\(cast\(address_of\(main::1::cw\), empty\*\)\)$
^ *FENCE WW RR RW WR$
^ *FENCE WW RR RW$
^ *FENCE RR RW$
^ *FENCE WW$
^ *FENCE$
--
^warning: ignoring
inline assembly statement at
ATOMIC_BEGIN
--
Pins the documented translation of recognized inline-assembly instructions by
the remove_asm pass (see doc/cprover-manual/modeling-inline-asm.md):
x86 mfence/lfence/sfence -> __asm_* fence helper calls; ARM dmb/dsb and Power
sync -> full fence (WW RR RW WR); ARM dmb/dsb with an ld option -> RR RW, with
an st option -> WW; Power lwsync -> fence without WR; Power eieio -> WW; ARM
isb / Power isync -> empty fence; nop/pause/yield -> nothing; fstcw/fldcw ->
__CPROVER_rounding_mode helpers called with the address of the operand.
See GitHub issue diffblue/cbmc#6374.
